ate over time meaning we need to  be quick to finish this fight of course  the only way to end this battle is with  a subtle bit of decapitation  that fight may have looked a little easy  that's where each Olga's abilities  behaviors and armor come into play  we are told these will be randomly  generated and will keep us on our toes  and unable to predict the August actions  in only a handful at previews we've  already seen around 30 different olgas  two fights to break that down a little  more of this Rivini has golden armor  which requires much more precise attacks  to destroy each latch additional time  will probably result in the augurs limbs  regenerating again adding to the  difficulty even the helm has two latches  before you can end the fight  the feeling of Shadow of the Colossus is  profound one tiny individual taking down  an enemy they seemingly have no way of  defeating some people also see  similarities with attack on Titan  probably due to the sheer size and scale  of the main enemy with Shadow of the  Colossus being remade for ps4 and attack  on Titan second outing coming in early  2018  this means this genre of giant killing  is highly competitive but all three  games have different elements which  distance themselves from one another  this is no longer  it is an entire nation  this soldier is all that stares  between humanity  and extinction  we've been a shot of a story-driven  campaign with many side missions once  all that is complete the skirmish mode  allows us to create battlegrounds and  challenge other players around the world  and extinction mode is basically a wave  based survival style game you've played  many times before  at present extinction is a single-player  title although with enough requests the  team have hinted there look into a  multiplayer option taking down a  colossus ogre with a friend sounds  absolutely epic to me so there you go  that six reasons to be excited for  extinction extinction is set to be  released in early 2018 and will be a  full-price title I have huge hopes for  this game and I am looking forward to it  but what about you fancy taking down a  150-foot monstrosity I'd love to know  your thoughts I'm Adam from Playstation  grenade I'll see you next time  [Music]
 

